-- title:
--   Ends of the blown-up supersingular chart: cyclic decomposition and crossings
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`), and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be, by (`hH₁`), the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ which by (`hK`) equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   **Base ring and chart.** Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-function (`hj`), let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hϖt`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$ one has $\varphi(j) \in$ [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Throughout, for $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ the phrase "$\tau$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$" abbreviates [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ ($p_g$ having nonzero image), every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the ratio of the images of $p_f$ and $p_g$, and every embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$, the coefficientwise $\iota$-image of the Laurent expansion of $\tau x$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\delta$ is the real matrix $\begin{pmatrix}\delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/q\\ q\,\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$. "$\tau$ preserves $W$" abbreviates $\forall f \in K:\ f \in W \leftrightarrow \tau f \in W$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-chart hypothesis `hArig`.** This hypothesis ranges over all points $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra along the middle chart) for which the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of $\varpi$, taken along `toBase`, lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, together with a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` whose prime satisfies the same supersingularity condition as $y$ above. For such data it asserts the existence of a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f\,u\bigr)$, subject to seven clauses: (i) $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if in addition $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for every such $\tau$ congruent to the identity modulo $y'$ there are an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwines $\tau$ through $e$, $\theta$ fixes constants, $\theta(X_{jj}) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M \equiv c\gamma$ and ($\gamma_{11}\equiv 1 \bmod \ell \Rightarrow c \equiv 1$) modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, while $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$ force $c \not\equiv 1$; (v) two primes of $S$ not containing both coordinates, containing $\sigma\varpi$, and having tangent directions $(a_1,b_1)$, $(a_2,b_2)$ with $q \nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, contract to distinct primes of the stalk; (vi) for a prime with tangent direction $(1,0)$, the germ of $a \in C$ lies in its contraction precisely when all Laurent coefficients of $a$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) a Hasse-germ clause: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $q$-fold substitution $j(\mathsf{q}^q)$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with $j_{q}-a_0 \in y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form takes unit values at every $(a,b)$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, such that $e$ sends the germ of $j_{q}-a_0$ to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The chosen point and its presentation.** Fix such a point $z$ with germ $\varpi_z \in \mathfrak{m}$ (`hϖz`, `hz`) and a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ (`hy'`) with the supersingularity property (`hss'`) and with $y'$ the prime $y$ (`hy'y`). Fix a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), power series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk at $z$ with $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$, such that (`hW₁`) exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) above hold for this data.
--
--   **Blow-up chart.** Let $J \subseteq C$ be, by (`hJ`), the intersection of all ideals of the form $(\tau|_C)^{-1}$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ(\text{completion})\circ(\text{germ at } y')$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ mapping $C$ into $C$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which by (`hB`) is the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, i.e. $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   Four further hypothesis groups are imposed. `hR1`: $C \subseteq B$, and every element of $K$ is a ratio of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator. `hR2`: $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): $W \cap L$ is the image of $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ iff $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$; and $W$ consists of the ratios $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses): (1) for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[x_0,x_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`) with kernel $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with $A \to k$, and such that for each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and each level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ there is $c \in \mathrm{GF}(q^2)^\times$ with $(\overline{\gamma},c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (i.e. $\det(\overline{\gamma})\,c^{q+1}=1$) for which $\rho\circ\tau$ equals `hAction` of $(\overline{\gamma},c)$ applied to $\rho$, and with $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (2) $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (3) every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is reached by some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau$, in the sense that every $b \in B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$ has $\tau b \in B$ and $\tau b \in Q$; (4) if $b \in B$ has $\tau b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ for all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all such $\tau$, then $\varpi \mid b$ in $B$; (5) a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, which preserves $y$ on $C$ also preserves $W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist: an integer $n \ge 1$ with $n \mid q+1$; an element $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau_0$ at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $W$; an integer $m \ge 1$ with $\varpi^m = \varpi_t\cdot(\text{unit})$; an element $\zeta_0$ of the adic completion $\widehat{A}$ with $\zeta_0^n = 1$ and $\zeta_0^k - 1$ a unit for $0<k<n$; proofs that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and an element $a_0 \in A$ with $j_{q} - a_0 \in y$; and a finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings of $K$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   1. $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B$ pointwise.
--
--   2. For each $0<k<n$ some $f \in B$ has $\tau_0^k f \ne f$.
--
--   3. Every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ agrees on $B$ with $\tau_0^k$ for some $k<n$.
--
--   4. $\mathrm{ends}$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   5. Every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ permutes the ends: for $O \in \mathrm{ends}$ there is $O' \in \mathrm{ends}$ with $f \in O \leftrightarrow \tau f \in O'$ for all $f \in K$.
--
--   6. Conversely the action is transitive: for all $O,O' \in \mathrm{ends}$ there are $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ with $f \in O \leftrightarrow \tau f \in O'$.
--
--   7. $\tau_0$ stabilises each end: $f \in O \leftrightarrow \tau_0 f \in O$ for all $O \in \mathrm{ends}$, $f \in K$.
--
--   8. Distinct ends are separated: for $O \ne O'$ in $\mathrm{ends}$ there is $f$ lying in both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$.
--
--   9. There is an $A$-subalgebra $B_c$ of $K$, of finite type over $A$, stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, contained in every end, and with each end $O$ the localisation of $B_c$ at the elements which are units of $O$: $f \in O$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of $O$.
--
--   10. For every $O \in \mathrm{ends}$: if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ maps $O$ into $W$, then $\tau$ preserves $W$.
--
--   11. For every $O \in \mathrm{ends}$: $O \subseteq W$, and $O$ is local and Noetherian, with $C \subseteq O$, $O \cap L$ the image of $A$, and for each $f \in O$ some $a \in A$ with $a \in O$ and $f-a$ a non-unit of $O$; moreover $\varpi \in O$ and there exist $c_x,c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ onto the crossing model $\widehat{A}[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \varpi^m)$, units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, an $\widehat{A}$-algebra automorphism $\theta_0$ of it, an inverse $\zeta_0'$ of $\zeta_0$, and a proof that the model is local, such that:
--    - $c_xc_y = \varpi^m u$ in $O$;
--    - $\iota$ sends the image of $a \in A$ to the constant $a$;
--    - $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V\,V$, where $U,V$ are the two coordinates of the crossing model;
--    - $c_y \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ and $c_x \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$;
--    - $j_{q}-a_0 \in O$ and, for some integer $e \ge 1$ and unit $w_V$, $\iota(j_{q}-a_0) = w_V\,V^{e}$;
--    - $\iota$ intertwines $\tau_0$ with $\theta_0$ on elements $f$ with $f, \tau_0 f \in O$;
--    - $\theta_0(U) - \zeta_0 U$ and $\theta_0(V)-\zeta_0' V$ lie in the square of the maximal ideal of the crossing model;
--    - there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K$ containing $O$ and $C$, with $W_x \cap L$ the image of $A$, $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ generated by $\varpi$, admitting $t \in W_x$ such that for $p \in A[T]$ with $p(t) \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ all coefficients of $p$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$, the same property holding for $j_{q}$ in place of $t$, with $c_x \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ and $c_y \notin \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$, with every $b \in C$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ already lying in $y$ and some $b \in y$ not lying in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$, with every other end $O' \ne O$ containing an element outside $W_x$, and such that if a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, maps an end $O'$ into $W_x$ then $O' = O$;
--    - there is an $A$-subalgebra $B_x$ of $K$ contained in $B \cap O$, of finite type over $A$, stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, whose elements $f$ satisfy $\operatorname{ord}_P f \ge 0$ at every place $P$ of $K$ over $L$ with $\operatorname{ord}_P j \ge 0$, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at the elements which are units of $O$, and containing an element $b$ with the following detecting property: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with $V \cap L$ the image of $A$, with $\varpi \in \mathfrak{m}_V$, with $j \in V$ and no value at $j$ of a monic polynomial over $A$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, and such that some element of $O$ is outside $V$, one has $b \notin V$.
--
--   12. Valuative covering: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with $V \cap L$ the image of $A$, containing $C$, and with $y \subseteq \mathfrak{m}_V$, either $B \subseteq V$, or there is an end $O \in \mathrm{ends}$ with $O \subseteq V$ and every non-unit of $O$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_V$.
--
--   This is the assembly step describing the exceptional fibre of the blow-up $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the $j$-finite chart at a supersingular closed point in characteristic $q$, in the variant where the auxiliary rigidifying level is the $\ell$-diamond condition for a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$: it produces the cyclic decomposition group generated by $\tau_0$, the $q+1$ ends of the exceptional Drinfeld curve with their $U V$-crossing presentations, the order of vanishing of the Hasse germ $j(\mathsf{q}^q)-a_0$ along a branch, Igusa-type valuation subrings separating the ends, and a valuative covering of the blow-up. It feeds the downstream assembly [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_supersingularAffineChart_ends_moduliHasse_commonChart_orbitPoles_inertia_chartAlgFin_of_stalk_drinfeldChart_moduliHasse_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_supersingularAffineChart_ends_moduliHasse_commonChart_orbitPoles_inertia_chartAlgFin_of_stalk_drinfeldChart_moduliHasse_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_dvd).
